# RustDAW credentials — copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own key.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. Never commit it, and never share it.

# Your own TONE3000 publishable key, used by the GET AMPS button to open
# TONE3000's picker and download the capture you choose.
#
# Get one by registering an application at https://www.tone3000.com/ — the key
# is yours, tied to your account. RustDAW does not ship a key and cannot use
# anyone else's.
#
# Register `http://localhost:3001` as the redirect URI for the application, or
# set TONE3000_REDIRECT_PORT below to whatever port you did register.
#
# Leaving this empty is fine: GET AMPS then simply opens tone3000.com in the
# browser so you can download captures by hand into `Amps/`.
TONE3000_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Optional. Only needed if you registered a redirect URI on a port other
# than 3001.
#TONE3000_REDIRECT_PORT=3001

# WARNING — do not add your TONE3000 secret key to this file.
#
# The secret key is a server credential. Anything compiled into a desktop
# binary can be read straight back out of it with `strings`, so a secret key
# placed here would be published to everyone you give a build to.
#
# The build script enforces this: it reads TONE3000_PUBLISHABLE_KEY and
# ignores every other variable in this file. Sign-in uses OAuth with PKCE,
# which needs the publishable key alone.
